{"findings":[{"id":"7cb90af9-b2d2-46a4-9866-f7bd7370a563","title":"Incomplete histories reach published notes","description":"`buildSite` treats `parseGitLog().malformed` as exhaustive validation, but the parser skips whitespace-only records and accepts a final record without its required terminator when its fields are otherwise valid. If either defect appears in the supplied stream, including a whitespace-only record before the requested commit, the build can succeed and write notes because its first-commit check examines the first parsed commit rather than the first record.","category":"Correctness","action_level":"remediation_recommended","attribution_status":"pending","git_sha":"ebb67dd424ddef2c6959e947ee10a396a201b1e5","location":{"file_path":"scripts/build-site.ts","start_line":81,"end_line":82,"side":"right"},"evidence":{"citations":[{"source_type":"pr_branch_file","source":"src/gitlog.ts[4-10]"},{"source_type":"pr_branch_file","source":"src/gitlog.ts[100-108]"},{"source_type":"pr_branch_file","source":"scripts/build-site.ts[81-96]"},{"source_type":"skill","source":"release-notes-audit"},{"source_type":"pr_branch_file","source":"scripts/build-site.ts[81-90]"},{"source_type":"pr_branch_file","source":"src/gitlog.ts[99-108]"}]}},{"id":"c03742ea-9d9c-426b-a89f-bf656739f3e0","title":"Failed builds leave incomplete site files","description":"`main` writes the four outputs directly to the destination in sequence, and its write-error handler does not remove files already created. If a later write fails, the command exits with an incomplete site that its non-empty-directory check rejects on retry.","category":"Reliability","action_level":"remediation_recommended","attribution_status":"pending","git_sha":"ebb67dd424ddef2c6959e947ee10a396a201b1e5","location":{"file_path":"scripts/build-site.ts","start_line":164,"end_line":166,"side":"right"},"evidence":{"citations":[{"source_type":"pr_branch_file","source":"scripts/build-site.ts[159-167]"}]}}],"finding_state":{"complet